1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:05,279
How to use the Mini-Grid Feasibility Calculator.

2
00:00:05,329 --> 00:00:08,079
By Emmanuel Boujieka Kamga.

3
00:00:09,629 --> 00:00:17,064
This calculator assesses a hybrid solar, battery and diesel mini-grid at pre-feasibility stage.

4
00:00:17,114 --> 00:00:27,050
It answers three questions: is the project viable on tariff revenue alone, can it carry debt, and how much subsidy closes the gap?

5
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:36,393
Open the Inputs sheet. You only edit the yellow cells with blue text; every other cell is a formula.

6
00:00:36,443 --> 00:00:43,593
Start with the project: life, hurdle rate, equity target, minimum DSCR, escalation and tax.

7
00:00:43,643 --> 00:00:49,436
Keep the hurdle rate and the escalation on the same basis, both nominal.

8
00:00:50,986 --> 00:00:55,850
Four multipliers stress the tariff, demand, CAPEX and OPEX.

9
00:00:55,900 --> 00:01:04,693
A value of 1.00 keeps your inputs as entered; 0.85 on demand simulates consumption fifteen percent below forecast.

10
00:01:06,243 --> 00:01:13,821
Enter each customer segment: number of customers, monthly consumption, tariff and connection fee.

11
00:01:13,871 --> 00:01:20,450
Then set the connection ramp-up, the growth in consumption and the collection rate.

12
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:28,079
Use survey or metering data rather than an appliance list, which usually overstates early demand.

13
00:01:29,629 --> 00:01:35,636
The calculator sizes PV, battery and diesel from energy sold in year three.

14
00:01:35,686 --> 00:01:43,336
Solar energy used at night passes through the battery, so round-trip losses raise the PV required.

15
00:01:43,386 --> 00:01:48,464
If you have a design, type your values in the Override column.

16
00:01:50,014 --> 00:01:57,093
Enter unit costs for PV, storage, generator, network and meters, then the operating costs.

17
00:01:57,143 --> 00:02:06,150
Battery replacements can be smoothed through a maintenance reserve, which keeps the DSCR stable in replacement years.

18
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:16,564
Describe the financing: upfront grant, RBF per new connection with its verification lag, and the senior loan terms.

19
00:02:16,614 --> 00:02:23,264
RBF arrives after commissioning and verification, so the developer has to bridge it.

20
00:02:24,814 --> 00:02:35,607
The dashboard shows project IRR and NPV before and after subsidies, the LCOE against levelized collected revenue, the DSCR and equity returns.

21
00:02:35,657 --> 00:02:43,736
Compare the LCOE with collected revenue, not with the year one tariff: both are discounted the same way.

22
00:02:45,286 --> 00:02:52,864
The viability gap is the upfront subsidy that brings pre-subsidy NPV to zero at your hurdle rate.

23
00:02:52,914 --> 00:03:00,564
In the example it reaches 907 dollars per connection, and the planned grant and RBF just close it.

24
00:03:00,614 --> 00:03:08,764
Five verdicts summarise bankability. Here the debt covenant is met, but equity returns stay below target.

25
00:03:10,314 --> 00:03:20,107
The charts show twenty years of revenue, OPEX and CFADS against debt service, and the split between solar and diesel generation.

26
00:03:21,657 --> 00:03:30,021
Before using any result, open the Checks sheet. Every line must read OK, and the dashboard must show ALL OK.

27
00:03:31,571 --> 00:03:39,579
The fifteen-page PDF manual details the method, the formulas, the worked example and the limits of use.

28
00:03:39,629 --> 00:03:45,493
Example values are illustrative: replace them with your own project data.

29
00:03:47,043 --> 00:03:53,979
You receive the workbook in English and French, the PDF manual and the integrity checks.

30
00:03:54,029 --> 00:04:00,679
The example values are illustrative: replace them with the data of your own project.
